    <h2>Where the idea was born.</h2>
    <p>The Netherlands is a country that made the sea itself negotiable — flat land reclaimed by patience and engineering, cities built around water instead of against it. That same practicality runs through Dutch style: no excess, no noise, clothes chosen because they work, not because they perform. It's a design culture that produced Droog, Dutch minimalism, and a national wardrobe built on quality basics rather than logos.</p>
